steps.change:
Insert a new `trend-ingest:` block directly after the existing `creator-copilot:` block, i.e. after line 515 (`theme-tag-batch-cron: ${CREATOR_COPILOT_THEME_TAG_CRON:0 0 3 * * *}`) and before the line-516 comment block for meera_interaction_log retention. Content:
  trend-ingest:
    enabled: ${TREND_INGEST_ENABLED:false}
    newsapi-api-key: ${NEWSAPI_KEY:}
    tmdb-api-key: ${TMDB_API_KEY:}
    youtube-api-key: ${YOUTUBE_API_KEY:}
All three follow the exact META_APP_ID/META_APP_SECRET precedent at lines 406-407 (blank, non-placeholder defaults — a REPLACE_WITH-style placeholder would be worse than blank because it would look configured). Do NOT add these under the existing `creator-copilot:` block (lines 507-515) — that prefix is reserved for CreatorCopilotProperties' own bound fields and mixing in unrelated keys would make Spring's relaxed-binding validation report an unknown/unmapped property warning at boot unless TrendIngestProperties itself gets extended (see risk about TrendSparkProperties above for why a separate class is cleaner).

Insert three pass-through lines into the influora-api service's environment: block (starts L123), after line 171 (`CREATOR_COPILOT_AI_BASE_URL: http://influora-ai:8000`) and before line 172's `# ---- Creator AI Co-pilot batch (OFF unless set in .env) ----` comment:
      # ---- TrendSpark trend-pull data sources (T4 ingest job) ----
      TREND_INGEST_ENABLED: ${TREND_INGEST_ENABLED:-false}
      NEWSAPI_KEY: ${NEWSAPI_KEY}
      TMDB_API_KEY: ${TMDB_API_KEY}
      YOUTUBE_API_KEY: ${YOUTUBE_API_KEY}
Uses the bare `${VAR}` (no `:-`) form matching META_APP_ID/META_APP_SECRET at L239-240, since an absent host .env var and an explicitly-empty one behave the same way here (blank -> feature silently off) — but note the file's own Q7.4 comment at L249-253 warns that Spring's `${VAR:default}` in application.yml only applies when the compose-forwarded value is ABSENT, not when it's present-but-empty, which is fine here since TrendIngestProperties.isConfigured()-style code (not SecretsStartupValidator) is what reads it.

trend-pull:
  enabled: ${TREND_PULL_ENABLED:false}
  cron: ${TREND_PULL_CRON:0 0 6 * * *}
  region: ${TREND_PULL_REGION:IN}
  max-rows-per-run: ${TREND_MAX_ROWS_PER_RUN:100}
  max-recovery-per-run: ${TREND_TAG_MAX_RECOVERY_PER_RUN:40}
  tmdb-api-key: ${TMDB_API_KEY:}
  news-api-key: ${NEWSAPI_KEY:}
  youtube-api-key: ${YOUTUBE_API_KEY:}
  recovery-secret: ${TREND_TAG_INGEST_SECRET:}
plus the four timeout/page-size keys. The env var NAMES are deliberately the ones the n8n cred store and docker-compose.yml L85-88 already use (TREND_MAX_ROWS_PER_RUN, TREND_TAG_MAX_RECOVERY_PER_RUN, TREND_TAG_INGEST_SECRET) so ops does not learn a second set.
